apps/mobile/live-activity-config.test.js guards the compact regions (lines 96-112) but nothing guards the expanded .leading/.trailing regions, which is how the edge-pinning bug in pump-pal-w9tq got in.

Append a mirroring block after the existing compact block:

  const expandedLeading = widgetSwift.match(
    /DynamicIslandExpandedRegion\(\.leading\) \{([\s\S]*?)\n\s*\}\n\s*\.contentMargins/,
  )?.[1];
  const expandedTrailing = widgetSwift.match(
    /DynamicIslandExpandedRegion\(\.trailing\) \{([\s\S]*?)\n\s*\}\n\s*\.contentMargins/,
  )?.[1];
  assert.ok(expandedLeading, 'expanded .leading region must be present');
  assert.ok(expandedTrailing, 'expanded .trailing region must be present');
  // These bands run to the display's rounded corner; edge-pinned text lands under
  // the mask. Centered (no alignment: argument) is the only safe placement.
  assert.doesNotMatch(expandedLeading, /alignment: \./);
  assert.doesNotMatch(expandedTrailing, /alignment: \./);
  assert.match(expandedLeading, /\.frame\(maxWidth: \.infinity\)/);
  assert.match(expandedTrailing, /\.frame\(maxWidth: \.infinity\)/);

The extraction regexes are a starting point, not gospel — verify they capture the right spans against the real file and adjust if they do not.

Leave every other assertion alone. The whole-file assertion at line 117 (/\.frame\(maxWidth: \.infinity, alignment: \.leading\)/) still passes: the .bottom region keeps that modifier legitimately at :243, :252 and :265.

Expanded Dynamic Island top row: set count renders as a clipped '9' at far left (0/1 swallowed by the display corner mask), and the row reads as shifted rather than balanced.

Root cause: apps/mobile/targets/widget/WorkoutLiveActivity.swift:220 and :230 pin their text to the OUTER edge of each side band:
  :220  .frame(maxWidth: .infinity, alignment: .leading)
  :230  .frame(maxWidth: .infinity, alignment: .trailing)

DynamicIslandExpandedRegion(.leading) occupies the band between the display's rounded corner and the sensor cutout. alignment: .leading drives the text to the extreme outer end of that band, where only .contentMargins(.horizontal, 4) (:224) separates it from the corner mask, so glyphs land under the curve and get cut. The trailing timer is pushed to the opposite extreme, which is what makes the row look shifted.

This is a DIFFERENT mechanism from the compact bug fixed in pump-pal-tq1x, even though the same modifier is involved. In compact, maxWidth: .infinity changed the pill's own size. Here the island is already full-size, so maxWidth only fills the band — it is the alignment: argument doing the damage, not maxWidth.

Fix: drop the alignment: argument from both, keep maxWidth. .frame(maxWidth: .infinity) defaults to alignment: .center, so the frame still fills the band and the text sits in the middle of it, clear of both the corner mask and the sensor cutout.

Add this comment above the .leading frame:
  // Centered, not edge-pinned: this band runs to the display's rounded
  // corner, and `alignment: .leading` parks the glyphs under the mask
  // (0/19 rendered as a clipped "9"). Center keeps clear of both the
  // corner and the sensor cutout.

Do NOT touch: the .bottom expanded region (:235-267, its spacing: 8 rhythm and .frame(maxWidth: .infinity, alignment: .leading) are correct — that region spans full width below the sensor with no mask to collide with); the lock-screen view; SegmentBar / ActionChip / ActionButtons; compactLeading / compactTrailing / minimal; .contentMargins(.horizontal, 4) on any region (centering removes the need to widen it).

apps/mobile/live-activity-config.test.js lines 104-112 assert the exact structure being removed (HStack, ProgressRing + count together in compactLeading, and both .frame(maxWidth: .infinity, alignment:) variants). They will fail after pump-pal-tq1x, and they are why the bad layout got locked in.

Replace that block with assertions that pin the fix:

  assert.match(compactLeading, /ProgressRing\(completedSets:/);
  // The pill must size to its content; maxWidth stretches it to full width.
  assert.doesNotMatch(compactLeading, /maxWidth: \.infinity/);
  assert.doesNotMatch(compactLeading, /\.padding\(/);
  assert.match(compactTrailing, /Text\("\\\\\\(context\.state\.completedSets\\)\/\\\\\\(context\.state\.totalSets\\)"\)/);
  assert.doesNotMatch(compactTrailing, /maxWidth: \.infinity/);
  assert.doesNotMatch(compactTrailing, /timerInterval/);
  assert.doesNotMatch(compactTrailing, /\.padding\(/);

